      "title": "SYRIA. Antioch. Roman Rule (after 65/64 BC). AE (25mm, 1h). NGC Choice Fine, countermark.  Dated Year 3 (47/46 BC). Laureate head of Zeus right; countermark of female head right in incuse oval / \u0391\u039d\u03a4\u0399\u039f\u03a7\u0395\u03a9\u039d \u03a4\u0397\u03a3 / \u039c\u0397\u03a4\u03a1\u039f\u03a0\u039f\u039b\u0395\u03a9\u03a3 \u039a\u0391\u0399 / \u0399\u0395\u03a1\u0391\u03a3 \u039a\u0391\u0399 \u0391\u03a3\u03a5\u039b\u039f\u03a5 / \u039a\u0391\u0399 \u0391\u03a5\u03a4\u039f\u039d\u039f\u039c\u039f\u03a5, Zeus enthroned left, Nike right in outstretched right hand, grounded scepter in left hand; headdress of Isis in inner left field, \u0393 (date) in exergue, all within a laurel wreath. McAlee 47. RPC I 4219.  From the Eyeappealing Collection. Ex Heritage Auctions, Auction 232322 (31 May 2023), lot 61100.  \"The coins of this year (Pompeian Era 19 = 48/7 BC) and year 3 of the Caesarean era are frequently seen with a countermark on the obverse which was previously described as \"head of Apollo r.\" in an oval...it now seems likely that the countermark portrays Cleopatra, and was used to mark coins circulating in the Syro-Phoenician territories which were given to her by Mark Antony.\" McAlee, The Coins of Roman Antioch, p. 74.   HID05401242017  \u00a9 2026 Heritage Auctions | All Rights Reserved www.HA.com/TexasAuctioneerLicenseNotice",
